# What the Markdown prose writer must not rewrite. That writer is the
# unwrap-markdown-prose-py hook in .pre-commit-config.yaml, and it reads this file
# itself rather than being handed an exclude list, so a bare CLI run in this directory
# honors these patterns too. This file is the whole definition: nothing else in the
# tree carries a second copy of the rule for it to agree with.
#
# Markdown that steers automation is not prose. A skill, a command, or an
# instruction file tells a write-capable agent what to do. Every one of them lives
# under a dot-directory apart from the two root files named below.
#
# `.*/` covers every dot-directory, including one added tomorrow -- `.cursor/`,
# `.claude/`, `.github/` alike -- unlike a bare `.*`, which would match only the
# root files.
.*/
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
